# Exclude large directories from Vercel uploads
# Dashboard fetches data from GitHub/S3 at runtime

# Course data (1.5GB+)
public/vfs/courses/*
!public/vfs/courses-manifest.json
vfs/

# Temp files (1.4GB)
temp/

# Logs (500MB+)
logs/

# Build artifacts (handled by Vercel)
dist/

# Development files
.env*
*.log

# Samples database
samples_database/

# Scripts and tools (not needed at runtime)
scripts/
tools/*
validators/
tests/

# ...except the ONE casting implementation. api/pod-cast-voices.js imports
# assignVoices from it, and a plain `tools/` prunes the directory so hard that
# the negation below could not re-include anything inside it — the route
# deployed and answered 500 FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED on every request
# (2026-08-11). `tools/*` excludes every child instead, which leaves the
# directory itself in place for the un-ignore to work, git-ignore style.
#
# Adding a second entry here is cheaper than a second copy of the casting
# rules. Anything re-included must be self-contained: pod-sync.cjs requires
# only dotenv, fs, path and @supabase/supabase-js, nothing else under tools/.
# The general rule still stands and is documented at api/pod-content.js and
# api/import-course.js — do not import tools/ from a Vercel function unless
# you also un-ignore it here and verify the deployed route live.
!tools/pod-sync.cjs

# Documentation (root docs/, NOT public/docs/ which is used in build)
# /docs/pods stays IN the upload: src/content/pod-thinking-docs.js imports from it at build time
/docs/*
!/docs/pods/
# ...but only the .md/.txt src/content/pod-thinking-docs.js actually globs — the
# JSON/PSV/CSV sweep logs that accumulate there (118MB, 2026-08-31) are not
# read at build time and blow the Vercel deploy past its 10MB request-body limit.
/docs/pods/*.json
/docs/pods/*.psv
/docs/pods/*.csv

# Archive
archive/
